Ingraham, Deia Williams, and Devine Rose (collectively,\n\u201cPlaintiffs\u201d) provide this brief submission in response to Defendant Capital One\u2019s October 2, 2025\nfiling to correct the record with regard to the events that resulted in Plaintiffs\u2019 September 30, 2025\nsubmission under Judge Thompson\u2019s standing orders in hope that the parties can avoid burdening\nthe Court with issues that do not move the matter forward, rather than focusing on the discovery\ndispute at issue.\n\n         During the September 29, 2025 meet and confer, I offered Capital One counsel the\nopportunity to participate in the joint briefing process. Rather than participating, Capital One took\nthe position that until it was willing to declare impasse (despite maintaining its refusal to produce\nthe at-issue discovery and offering no compromise to resolve the dispute), no joint briefing process\ncould go forward. I then informed counsel for Capital One that Plaintiffs intended to move forward\nwith the submission of this dispute to the Court, despite Capital One\u2019s refusal to participate in the\nJoint Letter Process and offered to include in that submission Capital One\u2019s position that the parties\nwere not at impasse. A lawyer for Capital One responded \u201cok\u201d, and Plaintiffs did include Capital\nOne\u2019s position in their September 30, 2025 submission. At most, the parties have a different\ninterpretation of what Capital One counsel meant by their statement \u201cok\u201d.\n\n       Plaintiffs take seriously the Court\u2019s instruction that future submissions follow the\nprocedures set forth in the Court\u2019s standing orders.\n\n\n\nDated: October 3, 2025                         Respectfully submitted,\n\n                                               /s/ J. Gerard Stranch, IV\n                                               J. Gerard Stranch, IV (admitted pro hac vice)\n                                               Counsel for PLAINTIFFS, VISHAL SHAH, GARY\n                                               INGRAHAM, DEIA WILLIAMS, and DEVIN\n                                               ROSE, individually, and on behalf of all others\n                                               similarly situated\n\n\n\n\n                                                  1\n\f       Case 3:24-cv-05985-TLT           Document 104        Filed 10/03/25       Page 2 of 2\n\n\n\n\n              ATTESTATION PURSUANT TO CIVIL LOCAL RULE 5-1(i)(3)\n\n       I, Lesley E. Weaver, attest that concurrence in the filing of this document has been obtained\nfrom the other signatories. I declare under penalty of perjury that the foregoing is true and correct.\n\n       Executed this 3rd day of October, 2025, at Oakland, California.\n\n                                               /s/ Lesley E. Weaver\n                                               Lesley E. Weaver\n\n\n\n\n                                                  2\n\f", "ocr_status": 2, "date_upload": "2025-10-04T10:23:19.430890-07:00", "document_number": "104", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "035026277688", "is_available": true, "is_free_on_pacer": null, "is_sealed": null, "document_type": 1, "description": "Discovery Letter Brief", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2025-10-03T16:06:39.171437-07:00", "date_modified": "2026-07-15T12:33:35.725370-07:00", "date_filed": "2025-10-03", "time_filed": "15:53:02", "entry_number": 104, "recap_sequence_number": "2025-10-03.001", "pacer_sequence_number": 312, "description": "Discovery Letter Brief Response to Defendant's Submission (ECF No. 97) filed by Vishal Shah, Gary Ingraham, Deia Williams, Devin Rose. (Weaver, Lesley) (Filed on 10/3/2025) Modified on 11/24/2025 (bxl, COURT STAFF). (Entered: 10/03/2025)", "tags": []}, {"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/439897493/", "id": 439897493, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/69088169/", "recap_documents": [{"re